Task: Add OrderEventPublisher (US-5.3, Phase 2)

Summary: order-service's first Kafka producer. OrderReservedEvent (local
mirror of the pinned order.reserved payload) + OrderEventPublisher, mirroring
payment-service's PaymentEventPublisher pattern exactly: fs2-kafka producer,
bounded retry via cats-retry (NOT purerest.resilience - confirmed Client[F]-
only, doesn't cover a Kafka producer call), log loudly and drop on
exhaustion. Kafka producer timeout properties (max.block.ms/
request.timeout.ms/delivery.timeout.ms) set to publishTimeout, matching the
fix payment-service needed for the same reason (the client's 60s defaults
block longer than a cats-effect .timeout() can actually interrupt).

Deviation from the original plan.md wording ("wrapped in purerest.resilience's
bounded retry"): corrected in conductor/tech-stack.md and
gluon/docs/system-design.md once it became clear purerest.resilience can't
wrap a Kafka producer call at all - this was discovered by payment-service's
parallel session building PaymentEventPublisher the same day, and confirmed
transitively available here too (cats-retry comes via purerestlib, same as
payment-service, no new build.sbt dependency needed).

Files changed:
- src/main/scala/orderservice/OrderEvents.scala (new - OrderReservedEvent)
- src/main/scala/orderservice/OrderEventPublisher.scala (new)
- src/test/scala/orderservice/OrderEventPublisherSuite.scala (new - 2 tests:
  happy path produces the event; unreachable broker exhausts bounded retry,
  logs WARN, doesn't raise)
- conductor/tech-stack.md (fs2-kafka note updated for producer side; cats-retry
  documented as a transitive dependency, deviation noted)

Tests: 2 passed, 0 failed.

Why: payment-service (US-6.1) needs order.reserved to know when to charge an
order - this is the one new piece of infrastructure (a Kafka producer) that
makes that possible, order-service having been consumer-only until now.
